tool: Go GoReSym -t -d -p | Rust rustfilt | .NET ilspycmd | jar javap -v -p / jadx | Swift swift-demangle\n  Nim nim-demangle | PyInstaller pyinstxtractor+pycdc | AutoIt autoit-ripper | anything else: rizin -q -c 'aaa;afl' /\n  analyzeHeadless (lib.binary.ghidra_decompile) | foreign arch: rizin -a <arch> / llvm-objdump-18 / Ghidra (no exec, qemu absent)\nHCFG (every new member since D2)\n  python: from lib.binary import hcfg_find, hcfg_scan; hcfg_find(open(F,'rb').read())  -> config, offset, encoding, key, crc_ok\n  raw magic 'HCFG' | b64 'SENGR' | hex '48434647' | rot13 'FRATE' | b64-zlib 'eJ' | b64-gzip 'H4sI' -> covered by hcfg_scan\n  accept only crc32(plain)==header crc AND JSON parses; keep scanning past decoys (D9 had two raw-magic decoys)\n  NOT FOUND => blob is hidden: (1) packed? unpack; (2) AES S-box 637c777b / TEA 9e3779b9 / 'expand 32-byte k' => find key+IV\n  near the call, decrypt with pycryptodome; (3) runs of mov [rbp-x], imm => stack-built: collect imms with capstone or\n  emulate the builder with unicorn; (4) PE .rsrc / .NET resource / jar non-class entry / overlay past last section;\n  (5) .init_array / TLS callback decoder => emulate it. Offsets: raw=the H, base64=the S (GM-confirmed); else first stored byte.\nFIELDS: format = container only (elf/pe/macho?/jar; .NET pe_cli) | machine/architecture = container machine word |\n  qualifier ids dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field> -> member whose file name has <tag> (D15 stripped/symbolized, D16 compact/direct;\n  match the LONGEST member-name token, a tag may contain `_`) ; sha256_K = zip archive order | config_* verbatim from HCFG JSON |\n  has_<x>_section = literal section name | hex fields lowercase 0x | never chase the prompt's theme: answer only asked ids.\n  D17 Ada ELF (GNAT 14.2), D18 Fortran ELF (libgfortran.so.5, MAIN__, *.f90): plain ELF, HCFG RAW in .rodata ->\n  carried-over solver answers it unchanged (D18 CORRECT at T+11 s). New language = expect ZERO new code; post first.\nTHEME FACTS (unasked so far, backfill candidates): every member D2+ embeds a huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1 JSON template\n  (branch, event_count, family \"<lang>_<theme>_trace\", effects, network) gated on env HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL (analysis/sandbox/\n  workstation). D18 flow: getenv -> _gfortran_select_string(case table jumptable.N.M) -> mov eax,<event_fn>; call rax.\n  Call graph: capstone direct call rel32 + resolve `call reg` from the preceding mov/lea imm; API intent from UND imports.\nBACKFILL ids on OLD groups (D8, D17): an unknown field on dNN = that day's own facts. Seen: marker (.huntress string),\n  recover_code (decimal imm), mangled_score_symbol/typeinfo_symbol (bare _ZNK.../_ZTI...; PE .text$/.rdata$), has_go_runtime,\n  has_rust_mangled_symbol, has_coroutine_runtime (enum true/false), methods (Main-Class method_info names incl <init>, JSON),\n  access_flags (decimal, 49), method_count (incl <init>/<clinit>). Derive from bytes, POST all derivable ones together.\nhcfg_storage (enum): base64 carrier -> base64 | literal HCFG in section `.hcfg` -> raw_hcfg_section | in WASM data seg ->\n  wasm_data_segment | in another native data section (.data/.rodata) -> raw_const_array | else raw. Stripped d01 => recover_code none.\nUNGUESSABLE label: ~10 single-id probes max, HELP.md, then re-pull the contract (organizers revise it: enum + rule text).\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"contract-revision-watch\", \"concept\": \"Organizers revise the live contract mid-day (D17: exact_text -> enum + rule text)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"When an exact_text label resists ~10 probes: write HELP, then re-pull the contract (`hctf status <id>`) every ~20-30 min and diff question text/answer_format per id; D17 the revision converted ~3.5 h and ~10.9k rejected probes into CORRECT within a minute. Never run mass automated label grouptests on a closed-vocabulary GM field.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"theme-facts-recording\", \"concept\": \"Record each day's (unasked) prompt-theme facts during the single solve so the later backfill answers without re-analysis\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NOTES.md under `THEME FACTS dNN:`; the solver's facts dict should already expose them as candidate field names.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"fortran-gfortran-deep-facts\", \"concept\": \"gfortran facts for the d18 group when its theme is backfilled: source file name, MAIN__, internal procedures (name.N), select_string case table, libgfortran imports, .comment GCC banner\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixtures: copy the cached d18 members (single variant-000 + TT/Mastery variants under challenges/day18/binary-flow-state/solver/cases/*/artifacts) into tests/data/binary_fixtures (gfortran compiler is NOT installed; runtime libgfortran.so.5 is). Facts: source_file `variant-000.f90` (STT_FILE), main_program `MAIN__`, procedures [event_failure, event_sandbox, event_decoy, event_success] with and without the `.N` suffix (table order + address order), case table = `_gfortran_select_string` struct array {low_ptr, low_len, high_ptr, high_len, case_no} x N (entry 0 = default, NULL ptrs) -> [(case_string, case_no)] e.g. analysis->1, sandbox->2, workstation->3, env var `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (the edi string passed to _gfortran_get_environment_variable_i4), imports list (9 `_gfortran_*`), NEEDED [libgfortran.so.5, libm.so.6, libgcc_s.so.1, libc.so.6], hcfg symbol `encoded_config.4`. Expose all as facts-dict keys with plain names (procedures, case_values, env_var, needed, imports, source_file).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"callgraph-indirect-flow-facts\", \"concept\": \"Generic call graph with indirect-call resolution for ELF/PE: per-function callees, PLT import edges, `mov/lea reg, imm; call reg` targets, call-table/jump-table targets, entry->main chain\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 prompt: 'Reconstruct the call graph ... follow the calls' (unasked). Implement lib.binary.call_graph(data) with capstone linear sweep over FUNC symbols (fallback: .eh_frame FDE ranges / rizin `aaa;aflj` when stripped): direct `call rel32` -> callee symbol or PLT import name (resolve via .rela.plt), `call reg` resolved by backward scan for `mov e/rax, imm32` or `lea rax, [rip+x]` in the same block, `call [rip+x]` via GOT/data pointer. Output edges [[caller, callee, kind(direct|plt|indirect)]] in address order, plus indirect_call_count, indirect_targets, functions_reached_from(main). Fixtures: d18 Fortran (4 indirect `call rax` to event_*), d01 C, d15 stripped/symbolized pair, a PE (d02 MinGW). Candidate GM shapes: JSON array of callee names, integer counts, `none` when stripped.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"api-intent-injection-classifier\", \"concept\": \"Classify each imported/called API by intent and give an injection verdict (ELF + PE), mapping to MITRE T1055.x\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 prompt: 'read the API intent at each edge, and prove no injection hides in the flow'; trace effects `modeled_process_access_no_injection`. Table (lib/knowledge.py-style dict, not lib edits by workers): env_query (getenv, _gfortran_get_environment_variable_i4, GetEnvironmentVariable), output (printf/puts/write/_gfortran_st_write*), string (strcmp/_gfortran_select_string/string_len_trim), process_access (ptrace ATTACH/PEEK, OpenProcess, /proc/<pid>/mem read), injection (ptrace POKETEXT/POKEDATA/SETREGS, process_vm_writev, VirtualAllocEx+WriteProcessMemory+CreateRemoteThread, NtMapViewOfSection, QueueUserAPC, SetWindowsHookEx, SetThreadContext, LD_PRELOAD/dlopen of a written file, memfd_create+execve), network (socket/connect/WSAStartup/WinHttp*). Facts: api_intents {name: intent}, has_injection (true/false), injection_apis [] , process_access_apis. Fixtures: d18 (no injection), plus small gcc/MinGW-free fixtures that import process_vm_writev / ptrace (PE: build import table with pefile or use existing PE fixtures).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dynamic-trace-template-facts\", \"concept\": \"Parse the `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` trace template embedded in every member (D2-D18) and model its env-gated branches\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every member carries a format template like `{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"<b>\\\",\\\"event_count\\\":<n>,\\\"campaign\\\":\\\"BRNN-00V\\\",\\\"family\\\":\\\"fortran_indirect_flow_trace\\\",\\\"effects\\\":\\\"modeled_process_access_no_injection\\\",\\\"network\\\":\\\"none\\\"}` (jar: constant-pool strings; wasm: data segment; some keys filled at runtime: manifest_entries, archive_score, selector `eventCountForModel:` on ObjC). Families seen: d10 non_mutating_service_plan, d11 synthetic_document_manifest, d12 private_scratch_archive_manifest, d14 non_mutating_trigger_plan, d15 symbol_loss_equivalent_trace, d17 ada_encoded_config_trace, d18 fortran_indirect_flow_trace. Extract per member: schema, family, effects, network, static key list, host-model options (`analysis`/`sandbox`/`workstation`), env var name (`HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`), and the branch/event chosen per option (static from the case table / compare chain; optional sandboxed run under bwrap with --unshare-net and the env set, ELF x86-64 only, never on the host). Facts keys: trace_schema, trace_family, trace_effects, trace_network, host_model_env, host_models, branch_for_<model>.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"hcfg-storage-classifier\", \"concept\": \"Generic `hcfg_storage` token for EVERY group/container per the D17 GM rule list (base64 / raw_hcfg_section / wasm_data_segment / raw_const_array / raw)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 asked it on d08/d09/d11-d14 only; the next backfill likely spreads it (as hcfg_offset spread) to d02 (ELF `.hcfg` or PE `.hcfg` COFF section), d03 (.NET FieldRVA blob inside PE `.text` -> by the rules `raw_const_array` only if the section is a data section, else `raw` -- record both as uncertain), d04 Go/d05 Rust/d17 Ada `.rodata` (raw_const_array), d06/d07 jars (base64 in a deflated constant pool -> `base64`), d10 `.hcfg` (raw_hcfg_section), d15 pair, d16 wasm (wasm_data_segment). Implement `lib.binary.hcfg_storage(data, hit)` = rules applied in order over (hit.encoding, container, section containing hit.offset with its flags: SHF_ALLOC && !SHF_EXECINSTR = data; PE IMAGE_SCN_CNT_INITIALIZED_DATA; Mach-O __DATA/__DATA_CONST/__TEXT,__const). Tests: every cached day02-day17 member on disk (GM-confirmed d08/d09/d11-d14 tokens as expected values) + synthetic `.hcfg`/.data/.rodata/.text/PE/wasm fixtures; return None (not a guess) when the hit lies in no section.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"question-rule-extractor\", \"concept\": \"Read the contract's per-id rule text + `accepted_values` and enforce it pre-submit (organizer revisions turn labels into enums)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17: the organizers re-issued the contract mid-day; hcfg_storage became kind enum with accepted_values and 'Apply these mutually exclusive rules in order: <token> when <cond>; ...; otherwise <token>'. Build a lane helper that (a) parses `(token, condition)` pairs out of such question text, (b) exposes `accepted_values` per id to the solver, (c) refuses to emit a token outside accepted_values (empty + log instead), (d) diffs two contract snapshots per id (question/answer_format changed) so a stuck worker sees the revision immediately. Tests: D17 single_solve morning vs revised contract.json (both on disk if cached; otherwise synthetic pair).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"offset-section-mapper\", \"concept\": \"Map a file offset to its container location: ELF section + segment (name, flags, VA), PE section (name, RVA, VA), Mach-O segment,section, WASM data segment index + memory offset\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Underpins hcfg_storage and the likely next location ids (`hcfg_section`, `hcfg_va`/`hcfg_vaddr`, `hcfg_rva`, `hcfg_segment`, `hcfg_mem_offset`). `lib.binary.locate_offset(data, off)` -> {container, section, section_flags, segment_index, vaddr, rva, wasm_data_index, wasm_mem_offset}; pure struct parsing (no pyelftools exceptions on sstripped files: fall back to program headers). Expected spellings to try first: section name verbatim (`.rodata`), VA as lowercase `0x` hex like entry_point. Tests on cached day08-day17 members (D17 Ada blob at file 207432 in `.rodata`, D14 at 4000 in `.hcfg`, D12 at 82928 in `.data`) and the wasm fixtures.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"elf-header-segment-facts\", \"concept\": \"Remaining ELF header + program-header facts as fields: e_flags, os_abi, abi_version, e_phnum/e_shnum/e_shstrndx, segments list (p_type order), interpreter, GNU_STACK/RELRO/PIE/static booleans\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"NOT BUILT (1st attempt killed rc -9, nothing written: keep the scope small -- pyelftools only, no Ghidra). Backfills so far asked elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, section_names, symbols, has_symtab. Next cheap carry-over ids: `segments`/`program_headers` (JSON of p_type names readelf-style `LOAD`/`PT_LOAD`? both recorded), `segment_count`, `section_count` (incl. NULL), `interpreter` (`/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2`), `os_abi` (`UNIX - System V` vs `ELFOSABI_SYSV` vs 0), `is_pie`/`is_static`/`has_nx`/`relro` (`full`/`partial`/`none`), `e_flags` hex. Implement in the solver facts dict (lib.binary helper) with GM-style spellings mirroring the confirmed ones (ET_EXEC style for enums, lowercase 0x hex, decimal counts). Tests: cached day01-day17 ELF members + readelf parity.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ada-gnat-deep-facts\", \"concept\": \"Ada/GNAT facts for the d17 group when its own theme is backfilled: GNAT version, binder/elaboration symbols, Ada subprogram names, decoder function, exception ids\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 prompt ('recover the reversible decoder') was unasked; the D17 backfill pattern means d17 facts get asked within days. From the cached Ada ELF (single_solve/work/extracted d17 member): gnat_version (`GNAT Version: 14.2.0` -> `14.2.0`), has_gnat_runtime (`__gnat_`/`ada__`/`system__`), main/binder symbols (`_ada_<main>`, `adainit`, `adafinal`, `__gnat_main`?), Ada-encoded names `pkg__sub` -> `pkg.sub` (keep mangled when asked for symbols), DWARF producer `GNU Ada 14.2.0` / DW_LANG_Ada95/2005, decoder routine name (function whose code xrefs the blob VA, via decoder-routine-locator) and its xor immediate (== header key?). Return none/false on absence; never raise.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"qemu-user-static\", \"concept\": \"Run/observe foreign-arch ELF decoders (ARM/AArch64/MIPS/PPC/RISC-V)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"apt install qemu-user-static binfmt-support (only qemu-system-* are installed now). Use only inside the bwrap sandbox, never on the host; static analysis remains the default.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"diec\", \"concept\": \"Compiler/packer/language fingerprint for unknown toolchains\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release horsicq/DIE-engine (die_lin64_portable tar) -> `diec -j F`. Complements `rz-bin -I` lang= and the STEP 3 strings regex when a new language lands.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"checksec-fields\", \"concept\": \"PIE/RELRO/NX/canary/static as answer fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"`rz-bin -I` already prints pic/relro/nx/canary/static/stripped. GM spelling unknown: relro full/partial/none, booleans true/false like has_symtab. Add to playbook naming law before first sighting; no checksec install needed.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-language-fingerprints\", \"concept\": \"Haskell, OCaml, V, Odin, COBOL, Modula-2, Kotlin/Native, Dart AOT, Nuitka (Ada seen D17, Fortran seen D18)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Cue strings are in the Recognition cues STEP 3 regex. All still answer format=elf/architecture=x86-64 per the D8-D15 law; risk is only where the HCFG literal lives (compressed Dart snapshot, Nuitka constants blob, GHC closures) -> hcfg_scan then Ghidra. Ada landed D17 as a plain ELF with RAW HCFG -- the law held. gfortran/gnat/ocaml/ghc are NOT installed for fixture builds (apt gfortran gnat ocaml-nox ghc if prebuilds are wanted).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"haskell-ghc-member\", \"concept\": \"Haskell (GHC) static ELF: z-encoded closures, rts strings, HCFG as a ByteString literal (raw or base64) possibly split across closures\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cues: `hs_main`, `ghczmprim_GHCziTypes_`, `base_GHCziBase_` z-encoding (zi = '.', zm = '-'), `GHC 9.x` rts banner, huge static binary, `.data` closures. Facts: has_ghc_runtime, z-decoded module names, ghc_version. Risk: a Text literal may be UTF-16 or chunked -> hcfg_scan utf16 + split modes. ghc not installed (apt ghc is ~1 GB): hand-craft fixtures with z-encoded symbol tables on a C ELF and a split-literal blob.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ocaml-native-member\", \"concept\": \"OCaml native ELF (ocamlopt): caml symbols, string literals with OCaml block headers, HCFG offset convention\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cues: `caml_startup`, `caml_main`, `camlStdlib__`, `camlDune__exe__Main`, `OCAMLRUNPARAM`. OCaml strings are header-prefixed blocks (word header + padded bytes, last byte = pad count) -> HCFG raw starts at the block payload (offset = the `H`, like D12/D14). Facts: has_ocaml_runtime, module names `camlMain__entry`. ocaml not installed: synthesize a C ELF with OCaml-shaped symbols + a block-wrapped blob.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"kotlin-native-member\", \"concept\": \"Kotlin/Native ELF (konanc): `kfun:` symbols, Konan runtime, HCFG in an object literal\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Kotlin already appeared as a jar (D7); a native build is a plausible 'pair the language with a new container' twist. Cues: `kfun:` / `kclass:` / `ktype:` symbols, `Konan_main`, `Kotlin_` runtime, `kotlin.native.internal`. Strings are UTF-16 in KString objects -> hcfg_scan utf16 path + offset = first stored byte (speculative). Facts: has_kotlin_native_runtime, kfun names. Fixture: C ELF with those symbol names + UTF-16LE base64 blob.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pe-optional-header-facts\", \"concept\": \"PE/COFF facts for the PE members (d02 MinGW, d03 .NET, d10 Zig PE, d04 Go .exe): subsystem, image_base, timestamp, characteristics, dll_characteristics, section names (NUL-trimmed), entry RVA/VA, imports\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"PE members re-roll into Mastery for d02/d04/d10; a backfill on them would ask the ELF-equivalent fields: format pe, machine, entry_point (ImageBase+AddressOfEntryPoint as 0x hex?), section_names (PE names, `/4` long names resolved via COFF string table), subsystem (`console`/`IMAGE_SUBSYSTEM_WINDOWS_CUI`/3), image_base, has_symtab (COFF symbol table present), timestamp (decimal). pefile installed. Tests: cached MinGW/Zig/Go/.NET PE members from day02-day16 artifacts + record both spelling families.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jumptable-switch-recovery\", \"concept\": \"Recover switch/SELECT CASE dispatch: gcc relative int32 tables (`movsxd rax,[rdx+rax*4]; add rax,rdx; jmp rax`), absolute 8-byte tables, MSVC/MinGW tables, gfortran select_string case arrays, Go/Rust match tables\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 dispatched on `_gfortran_select_string` + cmp chain; a stripped or -O2 sequel uses a real jump table. Implement lib.binary.switch_tables(data): find `jmp reg` preceded by a bounded index (cmp/ja) and a table base (lea rip+x), read N entries, map case -> target address -> symbol. Fixtures: clang-18/gcc -O2 C switch with 6+ dense cases (ELF + `-static`), the d18 case table, an AArch64 `br x` table (aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc). Output: [{case, target, symbol}] and case_count.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"anti-analysis-gating-facts\", \"concept\": \"Anti-analysis / sandbox gating facts: environment and host-model checks, decoy branches, debugger/VM detection (TracerPid, ptrace TRACEME, CPUID hypervisor bit, DMI/VM vendor strings, rdtsc timing)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 had event_sandbox/event_decoy branches selected by HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL -- an 'evasion' theme is a natural next day. Facts: anti_debug (bool + technique list: ptrace_traceme, tracerpid, isdebuggerpresent, ntqueryinformationprocess, timing), anti_vm (cpuid_hypervisor, vm_strings list), env_gates [env var names compared], decoy_functions (symbols named *decoy*, or branches that skip the HCFG). MITRE T1497 / T1622. Fixtures: small gcc C ELFs with each check (static analysis only; never execute).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"flattened-dispatcher-recovery\", \"concept\": \"Control-flow flattening (OLLVM-style state-variable dispatcher) and opaque predicates: recover the original block order / state transitions\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Title pun 'Flow State' -> state machine; OLLVM is not installed, so hand-write fixtures: C with `switch(state)` inside `while(1)` where each case sets the next state (constants xor'd), plus opaque predicates `x*(x+1)%2==0`. Extractor: identify the dispatcher (block with most predecessors + cmp/jmp on one stack var), emulate each case with unicorn to read the next-state constant, output the state sequence [s0, s1, ...], the executed block order, and the final return value (ties into emulate-return-value). Fixtures in ELF x86-64 and one MinGW-free PE via existing PE fixture style.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"gcc-frontend-modula2-member\", \"concept\": \"Next GCC front-end languages as a new-day member: Modula-2 (gm2), COBOL (gcobol, GCC 15), Algol 68 (ga68), gccgo\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 Ada and D18 Fortran were consecutive GCC front-ends (dynamic glibc, HCFG RAW in .rodata, carried-over solver answered both). Cues: gm2 NEEDED libm2pim.so.20/libm2iso.so.20/libm2rts, symbols `_M2_<Module>_init`/`_M2_<Module>_fini`/`_M2_<Module>_ctor`, `M2RTS_`; gcobol NEEDED libgcobol.so, `__gg__` symbols; gccgo NEEDED libgo.so.23, `__go_`/`main.main` symbols, `.go_export` section, NO `.go.buildinfo`; ga68 `libga68`. Install check: `apt-cache policy gm2 gfortran gccgo gcobol` -- build fixtures with an HCFG raw .rodata const array; confirm format elf / x86-64 and that hcfg_find + language_of return sane tokens (add the cue strings to language_of).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"de4dot\", \"concept\": \"ConfuserEx / .NET string encryption\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github de4dot-cex (ViRb3) release; needs apt mono-runtime. `de4dot F -o clean.dll` then ilspycmd.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"erlang-lua-decompilers\", \"concept\": \"BEAM, Lua, LuaJIT bytecode\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"luac (lua5.4) is now installed. Still missing: apt erlang-base (beam_lib/beam_disasm), unluac jar (sourceforge), luajit-decompiler-v2 (github marsinator358) -- only if a bytecode container appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"binutils-multiarch\", \"concept\": \"objdump/readelf for MIPS/PPC/SPARC/RISC-V\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"apt install binutils-multiarch; rizin, llvm-objdump-18 and Ghidra already cover disassembly, so this is a convenience only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ihex-srec-firmware\", \"concept\": \"Intel HEX / S-record / raw firmware members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"objcopy -I ihex|srec -O binary already converts (srecord not needed). For raw blobs: rizin -a arm -b 16 -m <base>; format label unknown (`ihex`/`srec`/`raw`?) -> submit alone.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cobol-gnucobol-member\", \"concept\": \"GnuCOBOL ELF (cobc): libcob NEEDED, cob_init, PIC X working-storage holding the HCFG\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cues: `libcob.so.4` NEEDED, `cob_init`/`cob_module_enter`, `GnuCOBOL` strings, program-id symbols upper-case. WORKING-STORAGE `PIC X(n) VALUE` literals sit raw in `.data` (-> raw_const_array) but COBOL source limits literal length (~160 chars) so the blob may be SPLIT across consecutive fields -> hcfg_scan split mode. Facts: has_cobol_runtime, program_id. gnucobol not installed: synthesize.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dart-aot-snapshot\", \"concept\": \"Dart AOT executable (`dart compile exe`): snapshot sections, HCFG inside the isolate snapshot (possibly compressed/obfuscated)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cues: `_kDartVmSnapshotData`, `_kDartIsolateSnapshotData/Instructions` symbols, `Dart_` runtime strings, ELF appended to dartaotruntime (or a standalone ELF in recent SDKs). Strings in the snapshot are stored as OneByteString objects (raw latin-1 with header) -> raw scan works unless compressed pointers/obfuscation; fallback search for SENGR base64. Record snapshot hash (32 hex) as a possible provenance field. No Dart SDK installed: synthesize an ELF with those symbols + OneByteString-shaped blob.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"backfill-language-identity-facts\", \"concept\": \"Per-language identity + theme facts for the D8-D17 groups (the next backfill): has_<lang>_runtime / has_<lang>_mangled_symbol / class, protocol, selector, proc, template names\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 re-asked D1-D7's single-solve facts on their old groups (marker, recover_code, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jvm-classfile-facts\", \"concept\": \"Full JVM ClassFile facts for jar groups (d06/d07): versions, constant-pool count, this/super/interfaces, fields, methods+descriptors, attributes, Kotlin metadata\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 asked methods (names, table order, incl <init>), access_flags (decimal 49) and method_count (incl <init>/<clinit>) of the Main-Class. Next backfill may ask major_version/minor_version, constant_pool_count, ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-metadata-facts\", \"concept\": \".NET metadata facts for the d03 group: assembly name/version, MVID, TypeDef/MethodDef names, FieldRVA, TargetFramework, entry point token\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). d03 is the only old group whose day-facts were not re-asked on D17 (it got hcfg_version/xor_key_hex only); a later backfill likely asks typedef/method names, method_count, assembly_name, assembly_version, ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"decoder-routine-locator\", \"concept\": \"Locate and characterise the config DECODER in the binary: function name, algorithm (xor/add/rol/rc4...), key/immediate, loop length, references to the stored blob\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 prompt: 'Recover the reversible decoder' (unasked, but a later backfill may ask decoder facts on d17 or any HCFG group). From the validated HcfgHit: compute blob VA, find code xrefs (RIP-relative lea/mov to VA in ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"native-imports-exports-facts\", \"concept\": \"imports / NEEDED / interpreter / exports lists for ELF, PE, Mach-O\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Generic facts: ELF `needed` (DT_NEEDED order), `imports` (UND .dynsym names, table order, version suffix stripped), `interpreter` (.interp without NUL), `exports` (defined dynsyms); PE import dll list + functions ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"provenance-facts-extractor\", \"concept\": \"Build provenance fields: GNU build-id, .comment compiler banner, DWARF producer/language/comp_dir, PE TimeDateStamp/PDB path/Rich, Go/Rust toolchain version\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Implement in the facts dict so a new id answers without code: build_id = lowercase hex of NT_GNU_BUILD_ID desc (no 0x), compiler = first `.comment` string, dwarf_producer via pyelftools, pdb_path from RSDS, timestamp as ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"language-detector\", \"concept\": \"lib.binary.language_of(data) -> source language/toolchain token with evidence, for all 17 seen languages + next candidates\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). A `language`/`compiler`/`toolchain` id on any group would need consistent tokens: c, cpp, csharp/dotnet, go, rust, java, kotlin, swift, nim, zig, d, pascal/fpc, crystal, objc, wat/wasm, ada; candidates haskell, ocaml, ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"emulate-return-value\", \"concept\": \"Recover a function's return value by emulation when it is not a `mov eax, imm; ret` leaf (obfuscated/computed/OLLVM recover_code)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). recover_code was re-asked D17; a mutated variant may compute the constant (xor of two imms, lookup table, flattened switch). unicorn x86-64 (installed): map the ELF PT_LOADs, set rsp to a scratch stack, run from the ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"api-hashing-resolver\", \"concept\": \"Imports r","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/00ba4211-f53f-4bd2-b67a-2bb0cc093ffa/tool-results/bm0jzim73.txt","persistedOutputSize":44526},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XmHDqCad4syBhpG5Dun8WV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
