{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NBEzUqC3Z7arDCDqJhdBKC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D18 post-run, 2026-10-18)\n2\t\n3\tScope: what a D19+ `evidence.zip` group (or backfilled old-group id) could be, how we would recognise it, which standard tool answers it, and how ready we\n4\tare. Grounded in `reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md` (lane log D1-D18), `challenges/day18/binary-flow-state/solver/`,\n5\t`lib/binary.py` (`hcfg_scan`/`hcfg_find`, `packer_info`, `unpack_upx`, `go_buildinfo`, `go_pclntab_funcs`, `rustfilt`, `macho_facts`,\n6\t`recover_return_constants`, `ghidra_decompile`, `jar_app_classes`, `wasm_layout`) and `tests/data/binary_fixtures/TARGETS.json` (all 9 targets have fixtures).\n7\t\n8\tProgression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86-64, HCFG blob re-stored per\n9\tlanguage); D15-D16 = \"ONE SOURCE, TWO BUILDS\" pairs with a `<qualifier>_` id prefix from the file-name tag (C ELF\n10\t`stripped`/`symbolized`; WebAssembly `compact`/`direct`, labels `wasm`/`wasm32`); D17 \"Decoder Ring\" = back to ONE new language\n11\t(Ada/GNAT ELF, HCFG RAW in `.rodata`, nothing new to decode) + BACKFILL #2 (160 -> 204 ids, 11 per old group) that re-asked\n12\tEARLIER DAYS' single-solve facts (d01 marker/recover_code, d02 mangled_score_symbol/typeinfo_symbol, d04 has_go_runtime, d05\n13\thas_rust_mangled_symbol, d06 methods/access_flags, d07 method_count/has_coroutine_runtime) and a NEW label field `hcfg_storage`\n14\t(an ENUM after the organizers' mid-day contract revision: base64 / raw_hcfg_section / raw_const_array / wasm_data_segment / raw,\n15\tpicked by an ordered rule list in the question text; before the revision ~10.9k free-text probes failed). TT/Mastery: d01 re-rolled\n16\tSTRIPPED -> `recover_code` `none`. **D18 \"Flow State\"** = ONE Fortran (gfortran) ELF, exactly as forecast (prebuild\n17\t`fortran-gfortran-member`): HCFG RAW in `.rodata` (`encoded_config.4`, offset 8512 in every variant), 216 ids = 204 + 12 new-group\n18\tids, NO backfill, CORRECT at T+11 s from the carried-over solver; TT/Mastery (4 sets) first try, d01 NOT stripped this time. The\n19\tD18 theme (\"reconstruct the call graph, read the API intent at each edge, prove no injection\") was unasked; the binary's flow =\n20\tgetenv(`HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`) -> `_gfortran_select_string` case table -> indirect `call rax` to `event_{decoy,sandbox,failure,\n21\tsuccess}` -> trace JSON (`fortran_indirect_flow_trace`, effects `modeled_process_access_no_injection`). Every member since D2\n22\tembeds such a `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` template -- a backfill can ask branch/event/family/effects facts.\n23\tLessons for D19+: (a) the next backfill will most likely reach D8-D18's own day facts (Swift/Nim/Zig/D/FPC/Crystal/ObjC/pair/\n24\twasm/Ada/Fortran identity booleans, symbol names, class/selector\n25\tlists, wasm imports/exports) -- the \"theme\" of a day is answerable LATER on its old group; (b) the new-day member keeps being a\n26\tplain ELF whose ids the carried-over solver already answers (D17 group banked at T+18 s, D18 at T+11 s); (c) label fields with no derivable\n27\tspelling (`hcfg_storage` raw, D3 `pe_cli`) are the real time sink -- and the organizers fix them by REVISING THE CONTRACT\n28\t(enum + rule text), so re-pull it instead of guessing; (d) location/storage-classification fields (`hcfg_offset`,\n29\t`hcfg_storage`) need offset -> section/segment mapping on every container. Asked field names: config_*, format, machine, architecture,\n30\telf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols, section_names, disassembly, marker, recover_code, has_symtab, has_cpp_*,\n31\thas_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol, has_coroutine_runtime, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, methods, access_flags,\n32\tmethod_count, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset, hcfg_version, hcfg_storage (enum), xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods.\n33\tRemaining risks: (1) more per-language fact backfills, (2) a twist that hides the HCFG from a byte scan (the D17 \"decoder\" theme\n34\tdid not materialise but stays plausible: packing, real crypto, stack-built, per-string encryption, API hashing), (3) a new\n35\tcontainer/arch label (Mach-O, eBPF, AArch64...), (4) more pair days with `_`-containing tags, (5) the D18 theme family as\n36\tfields: call-graph edges, indirect-call targets, API intent / `has_injection`, env-gated sandbox/decoy branches, trace family.\n37\t\n38\tTool legend: **[I]** installed (`source bin/env.sh`; checked with `which`/`ls`), **[M]** missing.\n39\tInstalled: readelf/objdump/nm/c++filt/strings/objcopy (binutils x86-64 + aarch64-linux-gnu-objdump), llvm-18 (llvm-objdump-18,\n40\tllvm-readobj-18, llvm-otool, llvm-lipo, llvm-nm, llvm-dwarfdump, llvm-cxxfilt-18 under /usr/lib/llvm-18/bin), file, binwalk, upx 4.2.4,\n41\trizin 0.9.1 (`bin/rizin`, `rz-bin`, `rz-asm`, `rz-find`, `rz-diff`) + radare2/rabin2, Ghidra (`bin/analyzeHeadless`, processors incl.\n42\tAARCH64/ARM/MIPS/PowerPC/RISCV/Sparc/x86/JVM/Dalvik), GoReSym, rustfilt, swift-demangle, nim-demangle, ilspycmd, dotnet, java/javap,\n43\tjadx, dex2jar, apktool, pyinstxtractor, pycdc/pycdas, autoit-ripper, hbc-decompiler, gdb + gdb-multiarch, ltrace/strace, yara, wabt (wasm-objdump/wasm2wat/wat2wasm/wasm-decompile), floss (.venv), luac,\n44\t7z, xxd; venv python: capstone, unicorn, angr, lief, pyelftools, pefile, dnfile, pycryptodome, pyzipper, xdis/uncompyle6/decompyle3,\n45\tlz4, yara. Cross compilers: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15, clang-18 (no lld/wasm-ld: other targets compile to `.o` only).\n46\tMissing: qemu-user(-static), wasm-ld/lld, wasmtime, capa, Detect-It-Easy (diec), de4dot, monodis, erlang (beam_disasm),\n47\tunluac/luajit-decompiler (luac present), blutter, srecord (srec_cat), binutils-multiarch, checksec, python zstandard/brotli, rzpipe/r2pipe.\n48\t\n49\t## Concept table\n50