nside the qualifier (`d17_analysis_x86_64_machine`): the router ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"wasm-inventory-fields\", \"concept\": \"WASM 'doors' as answer fields: imports, exports, memory min/max/shared/memory64, table + elem (call_indirect targets), start, globals, data segment count/offsets, custom sections\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). The D16 prompt named imports/memory/indirect calls but asked none; carry-over backfill may add them. Build fixtures with wat2wasm (installed): imports from env/wasi_snapshot_preview1 (func/memory/table/global), funcref ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ebpf-object\", \"concept\": \"eBPF ELF object (e_machine 247) with HCFG in .rodata / a map section\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). clang-18 -target bpf -O2 -c fixture with SEC(\\\"xdp\\\"), a `license` section, `.maps`, and an HCFG `.hcfg`/`.rodata` blob. Targets: format `elf`, elf_type ET_REL, machine readelf spelling `Linux BPF` (EM_BPF; integer 247), ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sstrip-corrupt-headers\", \"concept\": \"ELF without section headers (sstrip, e_shnum=0) or with bogus e_shoff/e_shstrndx/fake section names\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Fixtures: gcc build then python-zero e_shoff/e_shnum/e_shstrndx; another with garbage e_shstrndx; another with a section renamed to `.hcfg` that does not hold the blob. Targets: parser never crashes (pyelftools wrapped, ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"wasm-hcfg-hidden\", \"concept\": \"WASM HCFG not a plain active data segment: custom section `hcfg`, passive segment + memory.init, split across segments, built by i32.store immediates, UTF-16 (AssemblyScript), memory64 module\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Natural Mastery/next-day twist of D16. Fixtures via wat2wasm: (a) custom section named hcfg (has_hcfg_section analogue -> `true`), (b) passive segment