EGER (`64`/`62`)","-  on d08/d15 in ONE contract. Rule: dispatch on `kind`, not on the field name.","-- **Feature-presence fields** -- `has_<thing>_section` (D10, D14: literal section name `.hcfg`, PE names NUL-padded);","-  D17 adds runtime-identity booleans on old groups: `has_go_runtime` (d04: `\\xff Go buildinf:` / `.gopclntab` / `runtime.`),","-  `has_rust_mangled_symbol` (d05: `_ZN..17h<16hex>E` or `_R` v0 in .symtab), `has_coroutine_runtime` (d07: jar entries under","-  `kotlin/coroutines/`), `has_cpp_typeinfo/vtable` (d02, D8). Generic rule: `has_<x>` = a structural marker of <x> in THIS member;","-  expect `has_swift_*`/`has_nim_*`/`has_objc_*`/`has_gnat_*`-style ids on the D8-D17 groups next.","-- **Field set per old group** -- old groups gain ids over days (D8 padded to 10, D17 to 11 + hcfg_offset/hcfg_version spread to","-  every HCFG group). Answer by field name from the parsed facts dict of THAT member; unknown field -> log and fall through.","+  its FILE NAME. Rule: peel the longest field prefix that is a `[^a-z0-9]+`-separated token of exactly one member name. Tags seen:","+  `stripped`/`symbolized`, `compact`/`direct`; same HCFG in both. `sha256_K` = ARCHIVE order (central directory), never sorted.","+- **Variant index per group** -- `dNN--variant-XXX` re-rolls per group and mode; a carry-over d01 can re-roll STRIPPED (D15-D17","+  Mastery, D17 TT) -> symbols/disassembly `[]`, has_symtab `false`, `recover_code` `none` (D17 CONFIRMED; the leaf heuristic's","+  8106/8114 rejected); D18 not stripped; D19 TT d01 stripped again (`none` accepted). Pair by sha256, never index.","+- **Contract wording per fetch (D17)** -- the same id's question/answer_format can change between fetches (exact_text -> enum,","+  \"equivalents accepted\"). The solver reads `answer_format` per id at run time; assert enum tokens are in `accepted_values`.","+- **Mastery packaging** -- `setN.` prefixed ids, each set its own `delivery N: evidence.zip`: pair by sha256. Each set's 1s