EW `overlay_offset`\n(offset of the last magic) / `overlay_size` (file length - offset). The question text spelled the whole stub; 228 ids = 216 + 12,\nno backfill; CORRECT T+2:25, TT 4 s / Mastery (5 sets) 10 s first try; overlay 10808/424 constant across variants.\n**Forward hints in the D19 contract**: `overlay_offset` says \"PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20\" (=> D20 = another packed overlay,\nmagic `RS20`, probably a new language + a different stub); the `format` enum (d12-d19) lists `neko_bytecode` (=> a Neko VM `.n`\nmember is scheduled, magic `NEKO`).\nLessons for D20+: (a) read the longest question of each new family first -- since D17 the questions are executable specs (rules,\noffsets, transforms, hashes); (b) grep each new contract for tokens/days that are not today's (D19 leaked D20's magic and a future\ncontainer); (c) the new member's header ids keep being answered by the carried-over solver at T+~20 s, the day's twist is in the\nnew field family; (d) `none` is for ABSENT things, never for hidden ones (D19 race placeholders rejected); (e) unguessable labels\nare fixed by the organizers' contract revision -- re-pull instead of guessing.\nAsked field names: config_*, format (enum), machine, architecture, elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols,\nsection_names, disassembly, marker, recover_code, has_symtab, has_cpp_*, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol,\nhas_coroutine_runtime, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset,\nhcfg_version, hcfg_storage (enum), xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods, overlay_offset, overlay_size.\nRemaining risks: (1) D20 `RS20` with an unspecified or mutated stub (rolling key, RLE/LZ, RC4, multi-layer) -- the question text\nshould spell it, the solver must interpret it generically; (2) backfill on d19 asking the overlay header facts (k1, k2,\npacked_length, unpacked_sha256, overlay_version) or `hcfg_storage` for a packed blob; (3) Neko bytecode container labels\n(architecture/machine for a VM: unknown); (4) per-language fact backfills (D8-D19 groups); (5) the D18 theme family as fields.'''\nend = next(i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('Tool legend'))\nlines = head.split('\\n') + [''] + lines[end:]\ns = '\\n'.join(lines)\n\ns = s.replace('| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D18+ likelihood |',\n              '| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D20+ likelihood |')\n# COBOL row 24\ns = s.replace(\"| 24 | Niche native langs: Odin, Hare, Vala, GnuCOBOL, Chapel; other GCC front-ends: Modula-2 (gm2), COBOL (gcobol, GCC 15), Algol 68 (ga68), gccgo | gap (D17 Ada + D18 Fortran = two GCC front-ends in a row) |\",\n              \"| 24 | Niche native langs: Odin, Hare, Vala, Chapel; other GCC front-ends: Modula-2 (gm2), gcobol (GCC 15), Algol 68 (ga68), gccgo | gap (D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL = three 'legacy/enterprise' languages in a row) |\")\ns = s.replace(\"Odin `runtime.`/`__$startup_runtime`; Vala `g_object_`/GLib; COBOL `cob_init`, `libcob` |\",\n              \"Odin `runtime.`/`__$startup_runtime`; Vala `g_object_`/GLib |\")\n# Overlay row 57\ns = s.replace(\"| 57 | Overlay (bytes after last section / appended) | prebuilt (resource-overlay-hcfg) |\",\n              \"| 57 | Overlay (bytes after last section / appended) | **seen D19** (PK19 at e_shoff+e_shnum*64 = 10808, 424 B; `overlay_offset`/`overlay_size` asked) |\")\ns = s.replace(\"python `pefile` `get_overlay_data_start_offset()`; ELF: max(sh_offset+sh_size) vs size | med (raw scan already finds a raw/b64 overlay; a `has_overlay`/`overlay_offset` field would be new) |\",\n              \"python `pefile` `get_overlay_data_start_offset()`; ELF: image end = max(e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize, sh/ph ends) vs size; `data.rfind(magic)` | high (D20 `RS20` named; offset = the magic, size = len - offset) |\")\ns = s.replace(\"| 38 | Scrubbed UPX / other packers (MPRESS, ASPack, Themida, custom XOR stub) | gap |\",\n              \"| 38 | Scrubbed UPX / other packers (MPRESS, ASPack, Themida, custom XOR stub) | custom stub **seen D19** (PK19 ror/xor, spelled in the question); others gap |\")\ns = s.replace(\"| 37 | UPX packed | prebuilt (upx-packed-hcfg) |\", \"| 37 | UPX packed | prebuilt (upx-packed-hcfg; D19's 'unpacking' day used a custom overlay, not UPX) |\")\nnew_rows = '''| 81 | GnuCOBOL ELF (cobc, libcob) | **seen D19** (11 KB dynamic, stripped, old-GCC `.jcr`, `cob_check_version` string `1.5.2`, `variant-000.cob`) | NEEDED `libcob.so.1` + libvbisam/libgmp/libncurses/libtinfo/libdl/libm; imports `cob_init`, `cob_set_programid`, `cob_display`, `cob_get_environment`, `cob_stop_run`; host-model strings + trace JSON (`cobol_static_unpack_trace`) in `.rodata` | [I] `readelf -dW f \\\\| grep NEEDED`; `nm -D f \\\\| grep cob_`; [M] cobc (`apt gnucobol3` available) | high (carry-over; d19 theme facts = backfill candidates) |\n| 82 | Question-specified packer overlay (magic + keys + length + hash + byte transform) | **seen D19** (`PK19`: k1 +5, k2 +6, u32le len +8, sha256 +12, data +44, `ror8(b^k2,3)^k1`) | no crc-valid HCFG in the image; bytes past the image end start with `<2 caps><day>` magic; question text with \"Read k1 at +5 ... For each packed byte compute ...\" | [I] python: `o=data.rfind(b'PK19')`; parse header per the text; `hashlib.sha256(out)` check; known-plaintext `HCFG` fallback over xor/rotate | high (D20 `RS20` announced; expect a different header/transform) |\n| 83 | `RS20` overlay (Day 20, announced in the D19 contract) | gap | magic `RS20` past the image end; 'RS' guesses: RLE stream, rolling/stream-cipher (RC4/LCG keystream), reversed/rotated segments, Reed-Solomon-ish parity, resource-section | [I] python per the question text; `lib.binary.hcfg_scan` on the unpacked bytes; zlib/lzma/lz4 | high (named for Day 20) |\n| 84 | Neko VM bytecode (`.n`, Haxe -> neko) | gap (format enum lists `neko_bytecode` since D19) | magic `NEKO`, u32 nglobals, nfields, codesize, then globals (strings/floats/functions/debug), fields, code; strings stored raw -> raw HCFG scan likely works | [M] `apt install neko haxe` (both available: neko 2.4.1, haxe 4.3.7) -> `nekoc -z`/`neko -version`; python parser of the header + globals | high (in the GM's own enum) |\n| 85 | Other Haxe/VM targets: HashLink `.hl` (`HLB`), hxcpp native ELF (`hx::`/`__hxcpp_` symbols), Lua/Python bytecode via Haxe | gap | `HLB` + version byte; hxcpp `_ZN2hx` mangled symbols, `HXCPP` strings | [I] `.venv/bin/hl` exists (check what it is); [M] haxe | med (Neko implies a Haxe theme; more VM tokens may follow) |\n| 86 | Multi-layer / nested packing (overlay inside unpacked payload, decoy earlier overlay, packed ELF inside overlay) | gap (D19 said \"the FINAL PK19 overlay\" -> decoys/multiple overlays are in the generator's vocabulary) | several magic hits; unpacked bytes start with `\\\\x7fELF`/another magic instead of `HCFG`; sha256 mismatch on an earlier hit | [I] loop: rfind/finditer magic, verify hash, recurse on the payload (depth cap 4), HCFG scan at each layer | med-high |'''\ns = s.replace(\"\\n\\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\", \"\\n\" + new_rows + \"\\n\\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\", 1)\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nPYEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/atlas_edit.py && grep -n '^| 8[0-6] \\|^| 24 \\|^| 57 \\|^| 38 \\|^| 37 ' reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md | cut -c1-120","description":"Rewrite atlas header and table rows"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1741,"cache_read_input_tokens":136577,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1741},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_