{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBeW5Ng3c3F2tddQbjVB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017aP1kaw7UNMkkUEUpCzALQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; cat > $TMPDIR/atlas_edit2.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport json, re\np = 'reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md'\ns = open(p).read()\ns = s.replace(\"| [I] `.venv/bin/hl` exists (check what it is); [M] haxe |\", \"| [M] hashlink, haxe (`.venv/bin/hl` is an unrelated Python entry point, NOT HashLink) |\")\n# --- cues block\nold_cues = s[s.index('## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\\n```\\n'):s.index('## Readiness gaps')]\nc = old_cues\nc = c.replace(\"  0061736d \\\\0asm WASM (D16)\", \"  4e454b4f 'NEKO' => Neko VM bytecode: format `neko_bytecode` (in the GM enum since D19; unseen)\\n  0061736d \\\\0asm WASM (D16)\")\nc = c.replace(\"\"\"  NOT FOUND => blob is hidden: (1) packed? unpack;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  NOT FOUND => blob is hidden: (0) OVERLAY past the image end (D19): image_end = e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize (or max\n  section/segment end; PE: pefile overlay start); bytes there start with a day magic (PK19 D19, RS20 announced for D20) ->\n  o = data.rfind(magic) (\"final\"); parse the header fields the QUESTION lists; apply its byte transform (D19:\n  ror8(b^k2,3)^k1); verify its sha256; HCFG at out[0]. overlay_offset = o, overlay_size = len(data)-o; (1) packed? unpack;\"\"\")\nc = c.replace(\"\"\"  D17 Ada ELF (GNAT 14.2), D18 Fortran ELF (libgfortran.so.5, MAIN__, *.f90): plain ELF, HCFG RAW in .rodata ->\n  carried-over solver answers it unchanged (D18 CORRECT at T+11 s). New language = expect ZERO new code; post first.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL (libcob.so.1, cob_* imports, *.cob): plain ELF -> header ids from the carried-over\n  solver (post first, T+~20 s). The day's twist sits in the NEW field family: read its longest question first -- since D17\n  the question text is an executable spec (rules, offsets, transforms, hashes). `none` only for ABSENT things.\"\"\")\nc = c.replace(\"UNGUESSABLE label: ~10 single-id probes max, HELP.md, then re-pull the contract (organizers revise it: enum + rule text).\",\n\"\"\"UNGUESSABLE label: ~10 single-id probes max, HELP.md, then re-pull the contract (organizers revise it: enum + rule text).\nFORWARD HINTS: grep each new contract for tokens/days that are not today's (D19: `RS20 for Day 20`, enum `neko_bytecode`).\"\"\")\ns = s.replace(old_cues, c)\n# --- gaps json\na = s.index('## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n') + len('## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n')\nb = s.index('\\n```', a)\ngaps = json.loads(s[a:b])\ngaps = [g for g in gaps if g['id'] != 'cobol-gnucobol-member']\nby = {g['id']: g for g in gaps}\nby['theme-facts-recording']['detail'] = (\"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D19's WAS (overlay_offset/overlay_size + config only after \"\n  \"unpacking) and D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (stub/overlay \"\n  \"header fields, call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NOTES.md under `THEME FACTS dNN:`; the solver's facts \"\n  \"dict should already expose them as candidate field names (d19: overlay_version, k1/k2 hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256).\")\nby['theme-facts-recording']['concept'] = \"Record each day's prompt-theme facts during the single solve (asked on its own day since D19, or in a later backfill)\"\nfor gid in ('fortran-gfortran-deep-facts', 'callgraph-indirect-flow-facts', 'api-intent-injection-classifier', 'dynamic-trace-template-facts'):\n    by[gid]['priority'] = 2\n    if not by[gid]['detail'].startswith('BUILT'):\n        by[gid]['detail'] = 'BUILT (prebuild-state ok). ' + by[gid]['detail']\nby['resource-overlay-hcfg']['detail'] = by['resource-overlay-hcfg']['detail'].replace('BUILT (prebuild-state ok). ', 'BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Overlay part SEEN D19 as a packed PK19 overlay (not a raw/b64 blob; see question-spec-overlay-unpacker); resource parts unseen. ', 1)\nby['gcc-frontend-modula2-member']['detail'] = (\"NOT BUILT (1st attempt failed). D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL: the organizers walk a 'legacy/GCC-family \"\n  \"language' list, each landing as a plain dynamic ELF. Remaining: Modula-2 (gm2: NEEDED libm2pim/libm2iso/libm2rts, `_M2_<Module>_init`/`_fini`), \"\n  \"gccgo (libgo.so.23, `__go_`, `.go_export`, NO `.go.buildinfo`), Algol 68 (ga68), gcobol (GCC 15 COBOL: `libgcobol.so`, `__gg__` -- differs from D19's \"\n  \"libcob). Keep the scope small: add the cue strings to lib.binary.language_of + synthetic fixtures (C ELF with those NEEDED/symbol names and a raw \"\n  \"`.rodata` HCFG); compilers only if `apt-cache policy gm2 gccgo` shows a candidate.\")\nnew = [\n {\"id\": \"question-spec-overlay-unpacker\", \"concept\": \"Generic overlay unpacker driven by the QUESTION TEXT: magic, header field offsets/widths, keys, packed length, hash, per-byte transform expression\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"D19 config questions said: 'Find the final PK19 overlay. Read k1 at +5, k2 at +6, packed length u32le at +8, the 32-byte unpacked SHA-256 at +12, and packed bytes at +44. For each packed byte compute ror8(byte XOR k2,3) XOR k1; verify the unpacked SHA-256 and use the HCFG record at unpacked offset 0.' D20 announces `RS20` with a likely different layout. Build lib.binary.overlay_spec(question) -> {magic, fields{name:(off, fmt u8/u16le/u32le/u32be/bytes[n])}, data_off, hash(sha256/crc32/md5, field), transform AST} and overlay_unpack(data, spec) -> (offset, size, header, out, hash_ok). Transform grammar: XOR/ADD/SUB (mod 256), ror8/rol8(x,n), NOT, nibble swap, index terms (i, i mod n, key[i % len]), previous-byte chaining (prev plain/cipher), reversed order, keystream words (RC4(key), LCG(seed,a,c)), followed by optional zlib/lzma/RLE decompress. Reject (return None) when the hash fails; never guess. Fixtures: the cached D19 member (single + the Mastery/TT deliveries if cached) and synthetic RS20-style overlays for each grammar item with their question sentences; the D19 solver's overlay_unpack/overlay_magic in challenges/day19/binary-jack-in-the-box/solver/solve.py is the reference.\"},\n {\"id\": \"rs20-overlay-candidates\", \"concept\": \"Day 20 `RS20` overlay (named in the D19 contract): fixtures and decoders for the likely 'RS' stubs\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"D19 overlay_offset question: 'Locate the final overlay magic named by this unit (PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20)'. RS guesses, each as a synthetic ELF + appended `RS20` overlay with a sha256 of the unpacked HCFG and a question-style sentence: (a) RLE stream (count,byte pairs / PackBits), (b) rolling xor stream (key = key*mul+add per byte, or key ^= prev), (c) RC4 keystream with key bytes in the header, (d) reversed + rotated segments ('reverse-shuffle'), (e) rotate-by-index ror8(b, i%8), (f) zlib/LZSS after a byte map. Ensure overlay_offset = last `RS20` start and overlay_size = len - offset still hold, and the known-plaintext fallback (out starts with `HCFG`, ver 1, len = packed_len - 12) recovers unstated keys. Feed every fixture through question-spec-overlay-unpacker.\"},\n {\"id\": \"neko-bytecode-member\", \"concept\": \"Neko VM bytecode member (`.n`, magic NEKO): container parse, globals/strings, HCFG location, labels for format/architecture/machine\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"The GM's own format enum (d12-d19 since D19) lists `neko_bytecode` = a Neko member is scheduled. `apt install neko haxe` (candidates neko 2.4.1, haxe 4.3.7) then build fixtures: a Haxe `-neko out.n` program and a raw `nekoc` program holding the HCFG as a string literal (raw bytes and base64 'SENGR...') -- plus `nekotools boot` (Neko standalone ELF = neko VM + appended bytecode, another overlay!). Parser: 'NEKO' u32 nglobals, u32 nfields, u32 codesize; globals (type byte: 1 var, 2 function, 3 string u16/u32 len, 4 float, 5 debug, 6 version), fields (NUL-terminated names), code. Facts: format `neko_bytecode`, globals_count, fields list, string globals, hcfg offset (start of the string payload = the `H`/`S`), has_neko_runtime; architecture/machine for a VM are UNKNOWN -- record candidates (`neko`, `nekovm`, `none`) and read the question text first. Ensure lib.binary magic dispatch and the solver's format() return `neko_bytecode` for raw .n and recognise a nekotools-booted ELF (format elf + overlay).\"},\n {\"id\": \"overlay-header-facts\", \"concept\": \"Overlay/packer header facts as fields for the d19 group (and RS20): has_overlay, overlay_magic, overlay_version, k1_hex/k2_hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256, image_end\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"D19 asked only overlay_offset/overlay_size + config after unpacking; the D17 pattern means the header fields get asked within days (or on the d19 group in a backfill). From the PK19 header: magic `PK19`, version byte 4 (1), k1 byte 5 / k2 byte 6 as `0x%02x` (like xor_key_hex), pad byte 7, packed_length u32le +8 (380), unpacked_sha256 = 64 lowercase hex (+12..+44, no prefix, like artifact sha256), unpacked_size = len(out), packed_sha256, image_end (e_shoff + e_shnum*e_shentsize) and overlay == image_end boolean, overlay_entropy. Expose in the solver facts dict with plain names (overlay_version, k1_hex, k2_hex, packed_length, unpacked_length, unpacked_sha256, has_overlay=true/false) and a generic hcfg_storage answer for a packed blob (rule list: no section contains it -> `raw`? record as uncertain; read the enum text). Tests: cached D19 member + synthetic overlays.\"},\n {\"id\": \"multi-layer-overlay-chain\", \"concept\": \"Nested / decoy overlays: several magic hits, earlier decoy overlay with a bad hash, payload that is itself an ELF or another overlay\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"'Find the FINAL PK19 overlay' implies the generator knows multiple overlays. Fixtures: (a) two PK19 blocks, first with a wrong sha256 (decoy), (b) a magic string inside .rodata (code that checks it) before the real overlay, (c) unpacked payload = a tiny ELF whose own overlay/HCFG holds the config, (d) overlay inside the overlay. Rule set: prefer the LAST magic whose hash verifies; recurse into a payload that starts with a known magic (ELF/PE/NEKO/PK19/RS20/zlib) up to depth 4; report layer count and per-layer offsets (overlay_offset stays the outer file offset unless the question says otherwise).\"},\n {\"id\": \"decoder-stub-emulation\", \"concept\": \"Find the unpacking stub in code and emulate it over the overlay when the question does NOT spell the transform (timed mutations)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"D19 prompt: 'Find the stub, watch it work ... statically'. The question spelled ror8(b^k2,3)^k1, but a mutated variant may only say 'unpack the overlay'. Locate: code that reads the file (/proc/self/exe open + lseek(end)/fseek) or references the magic constant (cmp dword, 0x39314b50 = 'PK19' LE), then a byte loop with xor/ror/rol/add/sub immediates; extract the op sequence with capstone (xor reg8, imm / ror reg8, imm / xor with a header byte loaded from [buf+5]) and replay it in Python, or emulate the loop with unicorn over the packed bytes (no syscalls: stub the reads). GnuCOBOL stubs are C-library calls (libcob arithmetic) -> fall back to the known-plaintext search: out[0:4]=='HCFG', out[4]==1, u16 out[6:8] == packed_len-12, over transform families {xor a; rot r; xor c} x {add/sub} x {index-dependent}; accept only with the header sha256.\"},\n {\"id\": \"cobol-gnucobol-deep-facts\", \"concept\": \"GnuCOBOL facts for the d19 group when its theme/identity is backfilled: libcob version, program-id, source file, NEEDED list, cob_* imports, COBOL runtime boolean\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"D19 member (cached: challenges/day19/binary-jack-in-the-box/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d19--variant-000.elf): stripped dynamic ELF, NEEDED libcob.so.1, libm.so.6, libvbisam.so.1, libgmp.so.10, libncurses.so.5, libtinfo.so.5, libdl.so.2, libc.so.6; imports cob_init, cob_save_call_params, cob_call_params, cob_check_version, cob_set_programid, cob_push_call_stack_list, cob_stop_run, cob_initialized, cob_fatal_error, cob_cmp, cob_display, cob_get_environment, cob_current_module, cob_unifunc; `.rodata` strings `1.5.2` (cob_check_version arg), `variant-000.cob` (source), host models, `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`, trace family `cobol_static_unpack_trace`, effects `memory_only_inert_payload_hash`, branches failure/decoy/success with event counts 1/17/22/39. Facts keys: has_cobol_runtime (true/false), cobol_runtime_version, source_file, program_id (cob_set_programid argument via the lea before the call), needed, imports. Copy the member into tests/data/binary_fixtures as the fixture; `apt gnucobol3` (3.2) is available for a second, newer-libcob fixture (libcob.so.4).\"},\n {\"id\": \"haxe-vm-targets\", \"concept\": \"Haxe family beyond Neko: HashLink bytecode (`HLB`), hxcpp native ELF, nekotools-booted executables\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"If Neko lands, the same Haxe source may come as other targets (a pair day: `-neko`/`-hl`, or 'one source, two VMs'). With haxe installed (apt haxe 4.3.7): `haxe -main Main -hl out.hl` (HashLink magic `HLB` + version u8; strings table holds the HCFG), `-neko out.n`, and `nekotools boot out.n` (ELF neko VM + bytecode appended; the bytecode overlay begins with `NEKO`, boot trailer `NEKO` + u32 offset at the end). Facts: format candidates (`hashlink_bytecode`? read the enum), string tables, HCFG offsets. hxcpp (needs g++ + haxelib hxcpp) only if quick.\"},\n {\"id\": \"packer-decompressors\", \"concept\": \"Decompressors used by real packers for overlay payloads: aPLib, LZNT1, LZMA raw/LZMA86, LZ4 block, LZSS/LZ77 custom, RLE/PackBits\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"A 'static unpacking' sequel (RS20 or Mastery mutations) may compress before the byte transform. Implement pure-Python aPLib (depack), LZNT1, LZSS (4096 ring, 0x20 fill), PackBits/RLE and LZ4 block (python lz4 installed) in lib.binary with try-order by magic/entropy; lzma.FORMAT_RAW with lc3/lp0/pb2 dict 64 KB for raw LZMA. Fixtures: compress an HCFG with each (aPLib via a Python packer implementation), wrap in an overlay header with sha256, assert round-trip + hcfg_find on the output.\"},\n]\ngaps = gaps[:1] + [{\"id\": \"contract-forward-hints\", \"concept\": \"The live contract leaks upcoming days: tokens and day numbers that do not belong to today\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\",\n  \"detail\": \"D19: the format enum on d12-d19 lists `neko_bytecode` (never seen) and overlay_offset says 'PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20'. Each day, grep the contract for magic-like tokens (`[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}`), enum values never confirmed, and 'Day NN' > today; record them in solver/NOTES.md and the coverage atlas so the prebuild targets them. The d19 solver already maps a `<2 caps><NN>` magic to the group whose day is NN.\"}] + new[:4] + gaps[1:] + new[4:]\n# reorder: priority then keep relative order\ngaps.sort(key=lambda g: g['priority'])\nassert len({g['id'] for g in gaps}) == len(gaps)\nfor g in gaps: assert set(g) == {'id','concept','priority','action','detail'}\nbody = '[\\n' + ',\\n'.join('  ' + json.dumps(g, ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps) + '\\n]'\ns = s[:a] + body + s[b:]\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\njson.loads(body)\nst = json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend = [g['id'] for g in gaps if g['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('binary-reverse-engineering:'+g['id'],{}).get('ok') or st.get('binary-reverse-engineering:'+g['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint('pending prebuild', len(pend), pend)\nPYEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/atlas_edit2.py; f=reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md; awk '/^## Recognition cues/{f=1;next} /^## Readiness gaps/{f=0} f' $f | wc -l; wc -l $f","description":"Update cues block and readiness gaps JSON"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":432,"cache_read_input_tokens":143509,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":432},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00ba4211-f53f-4bd2-b67a-2bb0cc093ffa","uuid":"e4b5388c-9d29-4dac-b2f6-5e499e78861c","timestamp":"2026-10-19T13:08:42.994Z","request_id":"req_011CgBeW4y7wc9usRNYNF6qp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017aP1kaw7UNMkkUEUpCzALQ":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; cat > $TMPDIR/atlas_edit2.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport json, re\np = 'reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md'\ns = open(p).read()\ns = s.replace(\"| [I] `.venv/bin/hl` exists (check what it is); [M] haxe |\", \"| [M] hashlink, haxe (`.venv/bin/hl` is an unrelated Python entry point, NOT HashLink) |\")\n# --- cues block\nold_cues = s[s.index('## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\\n```\\n'):s.index('## Readiness gaps')]\nc = old_cues\nc = c.replace(\"  0061736d \\\\0asm WASM (D16)\", \"  4e454b4f 'NEKO' => Neko VM bytecode: format `neko_bytecode` (in the GM enum since D19; unseen)\\n  0061736d \\\\0asm WASM (D16)\")\nc = c.replace(\"\"\"  NOT FOUND => blob is hidden: (1) packed? unpack;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  NOT FOUND => blob is hidden: (0) OVERLAY past the image end (D19): image_end = e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize (or max\n  section/segment end; PE: pefile overlay start); bytes there start with a day magic (PK19 D19, RS20 announced for D20) ->\n  o = data.rfind(magic) (\"final\"); parse the header fields the QUESTION lists; apply its byte transform (D19:\n  ror8(b^k2,3)^k1); verify its sha256; HCFG at out[0]. overlay_offset = o, overlay_size = len(data)-o; (1) packed? unpack;\"\"\")\nc = c.replace(\"\"\"  D17 Ada ELF (GNAT 14.2), D18 Fortran ELF (libgfortran.so.5, MAIN__, *.f90): plain ELF, HCFG RAW in .rodata ->\n  carried-over solver answers it unchanged (D18 CORRECT at T+11 s). New language = expect ZERO new code; post first.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL (libcob.so.1, cob_* imports, *.cob): plain ELF -> header ids from the carried-over\n  solver (post first, T+~20 s). The day's twist sits in the NEW field family: read its longest question first -- since D17\n  the question text is an executable spec (rules, offsets, transforms, hashes). `none` only for ABSENT things.\"\"\")\nc = c.replace(\"UNGUESSABLE label: ~10 single-id probes max, HELP.md, then re-pull the contract (organizers revise it: enum + rule text).\",\n\"\"\"UNGUESSABLE label: ~10 single-id probes max, HELP.md, then re-pull the contract (organizers revise it: enum + rule text).\nFORWARD HINTS: grep each new contract for tokens/days that are not today's (D19: `RS20 for Day 20`, enum `neko_bytecode`).\"\"\")\ns = s.replace(old_cues, c)\n# --- gaps json\na = s.index('## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n') + len('## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n')\nb = s.index('\\n```', a)\ngaps = json.loads(s[a:b])\ngaps = [g for g in gaps if g['id'] != 'cobol-gnucobol-member']\nby = {g['id']: g for g in gaps}\nby['theme-facts-recording']['detail'] = (\"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D19's WAS (overlay_offset/overlay_size + config only after \"\n  \"unpacking) and D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (stub/overlay \"\n  \"header fields, call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NOTES.md under `THEME FACTS dNN:`; the solver's facts \"\n  \"dict should already expose them as candidate field names (d19: overlay_version, k1/k2 hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256).\")\nby['theme-facts-recording']['concept'] = \"Record each day's prompt-theme facts during the single solve (asked on its own day since D19, or in a later backfill)\"\nfor gid in ('fortran-gfortran-deep-facts', 'callgraph-indirect-flow-facts', 'api-intent-injection-classifier', 'dynamic-trace-template-facts'):\n    by[gid]['priority'] = 2\n    if not by[gid]['detail'].startswith('BUILT'):\n        by[gid]['detail'] = 'BUILT (prebuild-state ok). ' + by[gid]['detail']\nby['resource-overlay-hcfg']['detail'] = by['resource-overlay-hcfg']['detail'].replace('BUILT (prebuild-state ok). ', 'BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Overlay part SEEN D19 as a packed PK19 overlay (not a raw/b64 blob; see question-spec-overlay-unpacker); resource parts unseen. ', 1)\nby['gcc-frontend-modula2-member']['detail'] = (\"NOT BUILT (1st attempt failed). D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL: the organizers walk a 'legacy/GCC-family \"\n  \"language' list, each landing as a plain dynamic ELF. Remaining: Modula-2 (gm2: NEEDED libm2pim/libm2iso/libm2rts, `_M2_<Module>_init`/`_fini`), \"\n  \"gccgo (libgo.so.23, `__go_`, `.go_export`, NO `.go.buildinfo`), Algol 68 (ga68), gcobol (GCC 15 COBOL: `libgcobol.so`, `__gg__` -- differs from D19's \"\n  \"libcob). Keep the scope small: add the cue strings to lib.binary.language_of + synthetic fixtures (C ELF with those NEEDED/symbol names and a raw \"\n  \"`.rodata` HCFG); compilers only if `apt-cache policy gm2 gccgo` shows a candidate.\")\nnew = [\n {\"id\": \"question-spec-overlay-unpacker\", \"concept\": \"Generic overlay unpacker driven by the QUESTION TEXT: magic, header field offsets/widths, keys, packed length, hash, per-byte transform expression\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"D19 config questions said: 'Find the final PK19 overlay. Read k1 at +5, k2 at +6, packed length u32le at +8, the 32-byte unpacked SHA-256 at +12, and packed bytes at +44. For each packed byte compute ror8(byte XOR k2,3) XOR k1; verify the unpacked SHA-256 and use the HCFG record at unpacked offset 0.' D20 announces `RS20` with a likely different layout. Build lib.binary.overlay_spec(question) -> {magic, fields{name:(off, fmt u8/u16le/u32le/u32be/bytes[n])}, data_off, hash(sha256/crc32/md5, field), transform AST} and overlay_unpack(data, spec) -> (offset, size, header, out, hash_ok). Transform grammar: XOR/ADD/SUB (mod 256), ror8/rol8(x,n), NOT, nibble swap, index terms (i, i mod n, key[i % len]), previous-byte chaining (prev plain/cipher), reversed order, keystream words (RC4(key), LCG(seed,a,c)), followed by optional zlib/lzma/RLE decompress. Reject (return None) when the hash fails; never guess. Fixtures: the cached D19 member (single + the Mastery/TT deliveries if cached) and synthetic RS20-style overlays for each grammar item with their question sentences; the D19 solver's overlay_unpack/overlay_magic in challenges/day19/binary-jack-in-the-box/solver/solve.py is the reference.\"},\n {\"id\": \"rs20-overlay-candidates\", \"concept\": \"Day 20 `RS20` overlay (named in the D19 contract): fixtures and decoders for the likely 'RS' stubs\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"D19 overlay_offset question: 'Locate the final overlay magic named by this unit (PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20)'. RS guesses, each as a synthetic ELF + appended `RS20` overlay with a sha256 of the unpacked HCFG and a question-style sentence: (a) RLE stream (count,byte pairs / PackBits), (b) rolling xor stream (key = key*mul+add per byte, or key ^= prev), (c) RC4 keystream with key bytes in the header, (d) reversed + rotated segments ('reverse-shuffle'), (e) rotate-by-index ror8(b, i%8), (f) zlib/LZSS after a byte map. Ensure overlay_offset = last `RS20` start and overlay_size = len - offset still hold, and the known-plaintext fallback (out starts with `HCFG`, ver 1, len = packed_len - 12) recovers unstated keys. Feed every fixture through question-spec-overlay-unpacker.\"},\n {\"id\": \"neko-bytecode-member\", \"concept\": \"Neko VM bytecode member (`.n`, magic NEKO): container parse, globals/strings, HCFG location, labels for format/architecture/machine\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"The GM's own format enum (d12-d19 since D19) lists `neko_bytecode` = a Neko member is scheduled. `apt install neko haxe` (candidates neko 2.4.1, haxe 4.3.7) then build fixtures: a Haxe `-neko out.n` program and a raw `nekoc` program holding the HCFG as a string literal (raw bytes and base64 'SENGR...') -- plus `nekotools boot` (Neko standalone ELF = neko VM + appended bytecode, another overlay!). Parser: 'NEKO' u32 nglobals, u32 nfields, u32 codesize; globals (type byte: 1 var, 2 function, 3 string u16/u32 len, 4 float, 5 debug, 6 version), fields (NUL-terminated names), code. Facts: format `neko_bytecode`, globals_count, fields list, string globals, hcfg offset (start of the string payload = the `H`/`S`), has_neko_runtime; architecture/machine for a VM are UNKNOWN -- record candidates (`neko`, `nekovm`, `none`) and read the question text first. Ensure lib.binary magic dispatch and the solver's format() return `neko_bytecode` for raw .n and recognise a nekotools-booted ELF (format elf + overlay).\"},\n {\"id\": \"overlay-header-facts\", \"concept\": \"Overlay/packer header facts as fields for the d19 group (and RS20): has_overlay, overlay_magic, overlay_version, k1_hex/k2_hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256, image_end\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"D19 asked only overlay_offset/overlay_size + config after unpacking; the D17 pattern means the header fields get asked within days (or on the d19 group in a backfill). From the PK19 header: magic `PK19`, version byte 4 (1), k1 byte 5 / k2 byte 6 as `0x%02x` (like xor_key_hex), pad byte 7, packed_length u32le +8 (380), unpacked_sha256 = 64 lowercase hex (+12..+44, no prefix, like artifact sha256),